INSERT INTO `mod_lore_codex_entry` (`ID`, `Kind`, `Zone`, `SortOrder`, `Faction`, `RequiredState`, `Title`, `Body`, `Sources`) VALUES
(419700, 0, 4197, 0, 0, 13, 'Wintergrasp', 'Wintergrasp is a frozen valley in west-central Northrend, ringed by the Borean Tundra, Sholazar Basin, Icecrown and the Dragonblight. Titan fortifications dot the land and elemental riches abound, and both make it a prize: elementals of air, earth, water, fire and shadow roam it, and even living plants. At its northern end stands Wintergrasp Fortress, which guards the way into the Vault of Archavon, and the Valiance Expedition of the Alliance and the Horde''s Warsong champions fight over it again and again, in what the call to arms names the Battle for Lake Wintergrasp. No victory here is more than temporary. Between battles one side garrisons the keep while the other gathers at a camp on the valley''s edge, and when war returns, goblin and gnomish engineers turn out catapults, demolishers and siege engines at workshops across the field. The Wintergrasp River cuts the valley in two, with three towers beyond it to the south, and even in the lulls soldiers of both sides scour the land for embers, bone, herbs and armor, and kill each other for them.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Wintergrasp (a frozen valley in western-central Northrend; borders Borean Tundra, Sholazar Basin, Dragonblight, Icecrown; ancient titan fortifications dot the landscape; earth, fire, water, air, shadow and life elementals; WotLK sections only); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Vault_of_Archavon (History, citing the Wrath-era zone page: an abundance of elemental materials and strategically important titan fortifications make Wintergrasp the focus of a tug-of-war); creature_text 15214 group 27 (The Battle for Lake Wintergrasp is about to begin; BattlefieldWG.h BATTLEFIELD_WG_TEXT_WILL_START, sent before every battle); quest 13181 reward text (a victory in Lake Wintergrasp); quest 13181 description (Valiance Expedition) and reward text (a victory, even a temporary one); creature_template 30739 Warsong Champion and 30740 Valiance Expedition Champion (the keep guards of each side); BattlefieldWG.cpp/.h: keep NPCs shown for the defender, outside NPCs at each attacker''s camp (5025,3674 and 5101,2186); six goblin workshops; creature_template 30400 Goblin Mechanic and 30499 Gnomish Engineer (Demolisher Engineer); quest 13539 description (across the Wintergrasp River, three towers to the south); quests 236, 13153, 13154, 13156 and the Horde counterparts (embers, armor, bone, herbs; slay the other side to take them); zone_areas 4197: Chilled Earth Elemental 30849, Whispering Wind 30848, Glacial Spirit 30846, Raging Flame 30847, Wandering Shadow 30842, Living Lasher 30845'),
(419701, 1, 4197, 1, 0, 13, 'Wintergrasp Fortress', 'Wintergrasp Fortress stands at the northern end of the valley, the prize every battle is fought for. Two rings of walls guard it, broken by a great gate and anchored by four towers at its corners. Within lie two goblin workshops that can never be taken from the defenders, the officers and quartermasters of whichever side holds the place, and portals to distant battlefields. Behind the keep''s innermost door lies the chamber where, in battle, an attacking army must claim the titan relic to win the fortress. Here too opens the way into the Vault of Archavon, which only the side holding the fortress may enter.', 'BattlefieldWG.h WGGameObjectBuilding (outer and inner walls, the fortress door and last door, four keep towers), WGTurret (tower cannon positions), WGKeepNPC (officers, quartermasters 32294/32296/39172/39173, battlemasters 15350/15351 and the battleground portals 32616-32625); BattlefieldWG.cpp OnBattleStart (Titan Relic 192829 spawned at 5440,2840 for the attacker, unselectable until the last door 191810 falls); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Wintergrasp (the Titan Relic sits in the Relic Chamber in the keep''s innermost area); WorkshopsData (KEEP EAST and KEEP WEST cannot be taken); Goblin Workshop gameobjects 192028/192029 inside the walls; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Wintergrasp_Fortress (two wall layers, outer wall with gates, inner wall protecting the keep, anti-vehicle turret alcoves); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Vault_of_Archavon (inside the fortress; only the faction that controls Wintergrasp may enter); gameobjects 192903/192904 (instance portal, 5489,2839, posarea 4575)'),
(419702, 1, 4197, 2, 0, 13, 'The Wintergrasp River', 'The Wintergrasp River runs east to west across the middle of the valley and splits the field in two: the fortress and the nearer workshops on its northern side, the southern towers and the two farthest workshops beyond it. Three crossings span it, the Western, Central and Eastern Bridges, linking the two halves of the battlefield. Between battles the banks are quiet but not safe: glacial spirits drift along the water, and saronite crops out among the stones.', 'quest 13539 description (travel across the Wintergrasp River and destroy one of the three towers to the south); posarea: Central Bridge 4576 at x 4500-4700 on the fortress line, Eastern Bridge 4577 at y 2400, Western Bridge 4578 at y 3300; towers and southern workshops at x 4350-4560, fortress at x 5160-5490; zone_areas 4576-4578: Glacial Spirit 30846, Saronite Deposit 189980, Rich Saronite Deposit 189981'),
(419703, 1, 4197, 3, 0, 13, 'The Southern Towers', 'South of the Wintergrasp River stand three fortified towers: Shadowsight Tower in the west, Winter''s Edge Tower in the south and Flamewatch Tower in the east. In every battle they stand with the army besieging the fortress, and they are built so stoutly that only siege engines can bring one down. Between battles they stand silent over the southern field, and whispering winds drift past their walls.', 'quest 13538 description (Shadowsight, Flamewatch and Winter''s Edge Towers; only siege vehicles can damage a tower); BattlefieldWG.h WGGameObjectBuilding south towers 190356 (4557,3623, posarea 4583, the western tower), 190357 (4398,2822, posarea 4582, southern) and 190358 (4459,1944, posarea 4581, eastern); creature_text 15214 groups 1-6 (southern, eastern and western tower damaged or destroyed); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Wintergrasp (three towers in the south belong to the attackers); zone_areas 4582/4583: Whispering Wind 30848'),
(419704, 1, 4197, 4, 0, 13, 'The Siege Workshops', 'Six goblin workshops build the siege engines of Wintergrasp. Two stand inside the fortress walls and never change hands. The other four lie out on the field: the Broken Temple in the west and the Sunken Ring in the east, nearer the fortress, and Westspark and Eastspark in the far south beyond the river. Each flies a banner that can be torn down and raised for the other side, and keeps a graveyard with a spirit guide, taunka for the Horde, dwarven for the Alliance. Goblin mechanics build for the Horde and gnomish engineers for the Alliance, turning out catapults, demolishers and siege engines for soldiers of rank enough to authorize one, while the parts last.', 'zone_areas 4538, 4539, 4611, 4612: Goblin Workshop 192030-192033, factory banners 190475/190487/194959/194962, Goblin Mechanic 30400, Gnomish Engineer 30499, Taunka Spirit Guide 31841, Dwarven Spirit Guide 31842; creature_text 15214 groups 11-26 (the Broken Temple, Eastspark, Sunken Ring and Westspark siege workshops attacked and captured); BattlefieldWG.h WorkshopsData (NE, NW, SE, SW and the two keep workshops that cannot be taken); zone_wintergrasp.cpp npc_wg_demolisher_engineer (catapult, demolisher, siege engine); npc_text 13761 and 14172 (only certified officers of the Horde or Alliance can authorize the purchase of a vehicle); npc_text 13786 (we''ve used all of the parts we can spare); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Wintergrasp (Broken Temple the western workshop, Sunken Ring the eastern)'),
(419705, 1, 4197, 5, 0, 13, 'The Cauldron of Flames', 'In the southeast of Wintergrasp lies the Cauldron of Flames, a burning hollow where raging flames and drifting cinder clouds roam among the rocks. It yields eternal embers, which the siegesmiths of both sides mix with coal to fuel their demolishers and siege engines. Between battles soldiers of the Alliance and the Horde come here to gather them, and as often as not they take the embers from each other''s bodies. The Horde''s Siegesmith Stronghoof tells his soldiers that if the enemy has already gone, they must fight the fire elementals until they find some.', 'quests 236, 13197 (Siege Master Stouthandle) and 13191, 13200 (Siegesmith Stronghoof) descriptions: the Cauldron of Flames in southeastern Wintergrasp, eternal embers mixed with coal to fuel the demolishers and siege engines, slay the other side for their embers, or fight the fire elementals; zone_areas 4584: Raging Flame 30847, Cinder Cloud 32522'),
(419706, 1, 4197, 6, 0, 13, 'Glacial Falls', 'Glacial Falls spills down the eastern side of Wintergrasp, cold water and ice where glacial spirits drift. The Alliance''s enchantress, Sorceress Kaylana, says her research shows that the armor of soldiers lately slain here comes away steeped in energy, and the Horde''s Hoodoo Master Fu''jin claims the falls can draw out a strong warrior''s soul, which he means to bind into his wards and jinxes. So both sides send soldiers to kill each other at the falls, and when no enemy can be found, they strip the armor of adventurers the elementals have killed.', 'quests 13153 and 13198 descriptions (Kaylana: armor of soldiers recently slain in the Glacial Falls becomes imbued with an incredible amount of energy; the armor of an adventurer slain by the elementals); quests 13192 and 13202 descriptions (Fu''jin: the Glacial Falls in east Wintergrasp has special properties to extract the soul; hoodoo wards, jinxing the walls); creature_template 31051 Sorceress Kaylana <Enchantress>, 31101 Hoodoo Master Fu''jin <Master Hexxer>; zone_areas 4585: Glacial Spirit 30846'),
(419707, 1, 4197, 7, 0, 13, 'The Forest of Shadows', 'On the western edge of Wintergrasp lies the Forest of Shadows, a dark wood littered with old dragon bones and haunted by wandering shadows. Some say the spirits impale their living victims on the bones as they die. The bones are useful all the same: with dragonbone grown hard to come by in the Dragonblight, the bowyers of both sides need splinters from this forest for their arrowheads, and their soldiers come hunting for them, and for each other. Bowyer Randolph of the Alliance has heard it is haunted, and admits he never goes there himself.', 'quests 13154 and 13196 descriptions and completion text (Randolph: dragonbone arrowheads, bone hard to get from Dragonblight, the Forest of Shadows on the western edge; rumors the place is haunted, I never venture out there); quests 13193 and 13199 descriptions (Vieron Blazefeather: the spirits impale their living victims on the bones as they die; the Alliance scavenge dragon bones there); zone_areas 4587: Wandering Shadow 30842'),
(419708, 1, 4197, 8, 0, 13, 'The Steppe of Life', 'In the southwest of Wintergrasp, the Steppe of Life is a stretch of ground where things still grow despite the cold, guarded by living lashers that whip at anyone who comes too close. Both sides'' healers depend on it. The Horde''s Primalist Mulfort makes salve for the wounded from the roses that grow here, and the Alliance''s Anchorite Tessa grinds its herbs into a medicine against the cold. Mulfort complains that the Alliance strips the roses too fast, Tessa that the Horde has been gathering the herbs, so soldiers come to gather and stay to kill one another, and Tessa still warns of the lashers that gave a Private Doane a fine whipping.', 'quests 13194 and 13201 descriptions (Mulfort: roses of the Steppe of Life in southwestern Wintergrasp for salve; scarce because the Alliance harvest it too rapidly; a lasher might have one); quests 13156 and 13195 descriptions and completion text (Tessa: herbs ground into medicine against the cold; the Horde collect them; lashers gave Private Doane quite a whipping); zone_areas 4590: Living Lasher 30845'),
(419710, 2, 4197, 1, 1, 13, 'Commander Zanneth', 'Commander Zanneth leads the Alliance''s fighters in Wintergrasp. He greets each newcomer as one come to serve the sons of Azeroth in battle, and whether he stands in the fortress or at the camp from which the Alliance marches on it, his orders never change: go out, defeat ten of the Horde''s finest, and come back. Not all his officers think that enough. Tactical Officer Ahbramis grumbles that the commander might be content with a pile of Horde corpses at his feet, while what matters to the Valiance Expedition is who holds Wintergrasp.', 'npc_text 14238 (Hail, friend! Have you come to serve the sons of Azeroth in battle?); quests 13177 and 13179 descriptions and reward text (defeat ten of the Horde''s finest); quest 13181 description (Ahbramis: Commander Zanneth might be satisfied with a pile of Horde corpses at his feet; controlling Wintergrasp matters to the Valiance Expedition); BattlefieldWG.h WGKeepNPC and WGOutsideNPC (Zanneth 31036 in the keep while the Alliance defends, at the Alliance camp at 5078,2183 while it attacks)'),
(419711, 2, 4197, 2, 2, 13, 'Commander Dardosh', 'Commander Dardosh leads the Horde''s fighters in Wintergrasp, and he greets each newcomer with a war cry and a question: have they come to serve the Horde in battle? Whether he stands in the fortress or at the camp from which the Horde marches on it, he carries Warlord Garrosh''s orders, and Garrosh asks only one thing: that every foe be slain. Every recruit is sent out to bring down ten of the Alliance''s strongest. Tactical Officer Kilrath, at his side, takes a longer view: Dardosh may be content with slain foes, but what matters to Kilrath is holding the fortress itself.', 'npc_text 14221 (Lok''tar! Have you come to serve the Horde in battle?); quests 13178 and 13180 descriptions and reward text (Warlord Garrosh demands one thing: slay them all; ten of the strongest members of the Alliance); quest 13183 description (Kilrath: while Dardosh might be content with slaying our foes, it is of the utmost importance that we control Wintergrasp Fortress); BattlefieldWG.h WGKeepNPC and WGOutsideNPC (Dardosh 31091 in the keep while the Horde defends, at the Horde camp at 4994,3660 while it attacks)'),
(419720, 3, 4197, 1, 0, 13, 'The Battle for Wintergrasp', 'At set times the war for Wintergrasp breaks out anew. The defenders muster inside the fortress, while the attackers gather at their camp and march on it. The workshops pour out siege engines, and each side''s officers give their soldiers the task their role demands. The attackers must crew and guard their machines while they smash wall after wall; the Alliance trusts in what Senior Demolitionist Legoso calls the power of gnomish technology, and the Horde''s Lieutenant Murp wishes he could leave camp to smash walls himself. The defenders must wreck those machines before they break through. The attackers'' goal lies deep in the keep, where they must claim the titan relic before time runs out; if they fail, the fortress stays in the defenders'' hands.', 'quests 13222 and 13223 descriptions (Legoso: the power of Gnomish technology, smash their walls; pilot or protect a siege vehicle as it destroys three structures; Murp: has to stay in camp, wishes he could smash walls); quests 13185 and 13186 descriptions (destroy three enemy siege devices); quests 13181 and 13183 descriptions (win the battle; control of the fortress matters most); BattlefieldWG.cpp OnBattleStart and OnBattleEnd (relic spawned for the attackers, unselectable until the last door falls; a battle ended by the timer leaves the defenders in possession); OnPlayerJoinWar (defenders sent into the keep, attackers to their camps); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Wintergrasp (Relic Chamber in the keep''s innermost area)'),
(419721, 3, 4197, 2, 0, 13, 'The Elementals of Wintergrasp', 'Wintergrasp swarms with elementals. Chilled earth elementals lumber across the open valley, and glacial spirits haunt the river, the falls and the Chilled Quagmire. Whispering winds drift through the south, raging flames and cinder clouds burn in the Cauldron of Flames, wandering shadows stalk the Forest of Shadows, and living lashers guard the Steppe of Life. They answer to neither the Alliance nor the Horde and turn on whoever strays near them, so anyone who crosses the valley between battles must reckon with them as well as with the enemy.', 'zone_areas 4197 and subzones: Chilled Earth Elemental 30849, Glacial Spirit 30846 (bridges, Glacial Falls, Chilled Quagmire), Whispering Wind 30848 (Winter''s Edge and Shadowsight Towers; spawns centred on x 4206), Raging Flame 30847 and Cinder Cloud 32522 (Cauldron of Flames), Wandering Shadow 30842 (Forest of Shadows), Living Lasher 30845 (Steppe of Life); all phase 1; creature_template factions 14, 834, 91, 21, 16 (hostile monsters); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Wintergrasp (wandering air, earth, fire, water, shadow and life elementals)');
INSERT INTO `mod_lore_codex_part` (`Entry`, `Part`, `MinState`, `MaxState`, `Body`, `Sources`) VALUES
(419703, 1, 0, 255, 'The towers are more than strongpoints. The officers of the fortress say they draw power away from it, and when one is brought down that power can be turned back into the titan relic to strengthen the fortress''s own soldiers. So the defenders do not simply wait behind their walls: they cross the river and topple a tower where the attackers least expect it.', 'quest 13538 description (the towers are draining power from the Fortress) and reward text (rerouting the power into the Titan relic to super-charge our own forces); quest 13539 description (attack where he is unprepared; the towers drain power we could use to bolster our own troops)'),
(419720, 1, 0, 255, 'A victory in Wintergrasp has been won, and it will not be the last battle. Whoever holds the fortress must hold it again when the war returns, and whoever lost it will come back for it. The Alliance''s officers count even a passing victory crucial to their whole strategy against the Horde, and the Horde''s officers honor those who fought for it as having done a truly great thing.', 'quest 13181 reward text (a victory in Lake Wintergrasp, even a temporary one, is crucial to our overall strategy against the Horde); quest 13183 reward text (a truly great thing you have accomplished; be recognized for your sacrifice)'),
(419721, 1, 0, 255, 'The elementals are part of why the valley is worth fighting for, since it is rich in elemental materials. Between battles both armies send soldiers out to gather: embers from the fire, armor from the falls, bone from the shadowed forest and herbs from the lashers'' steppe. The quartermasters would rather their soldiers took these things from enemy bodies, but when no enemy is about, the elementals and their victims will serve.', 'quests 13153, 13198, 13192, 13202 (armor of adventurers slain by the elementals), 13191, 13200 (fight the fire elementals for embers), 13193, 13199 (bones from the spirits), 13195, 13194, 13201 (a lasher might have one); every gathering quest asks first for the enemy''s bodies; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Vault_of_Archavon (History, Wrath-era zone page: an abundance of elemental materials)');
